  "id": "Compound::DB00334 - Gene::1812",
  "verbalization": "Olanzapine is implicated in the activation of Drd1 through multiple indirect pathways involving G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptors. The drug binds to Hrh4, which participates in G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity, and this activity is linked to Drd1. Similarly, Olanzapine binds to Htr5a, which is involved in monoamine GPCR activity, also leading to Drd1 activation. These pathways suggest that Olanzapine exerts its effects on Drd1 via receptor activation through different GPCR subtypes. The evidence highlights a mechanism where Olanzapine influences Drd1 through the modulation of GPCR activity, though the exact nature of the receptor interaction remains unspecified. The integration of these pathways underscores a potential role for Olanzapine in modulating Drd1 function through receptor-mediated signaling, emphasizing the importance of GPCR involvement in its pharmacological profile.",
